  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Open Face Chinese Poker. 52 cards, 2-4 players. Partition 13 cards into Back 5, Middle 5, Front 3. Back â‰¥ Middle â‰¥ Front or foul (pay 6). 1 pt per hand, 3 pt sweep, royalties. Fantasyland: QQ+ Front = 13 cards next hand.',
    Player: 'You have Back: Kâ™ Kâ™¥Kâ™¦Qâ™£9â™ , Middle: Aâ™ Aâ™¥7â™¦6â™£2â™¥, Front: Jâ™ Jâ™¥. You draw 3â™¦. Place it in Middle (keeps Back > Middle > Front) or risk fouling.',
    objective: 'Score more points than opponents by winning hand comparisons and earning royalties. Avoid fouling (Back < Middle or Middle < Front).',
    gameplay: '1. **Initial deal**: 5 cards each, set face-up into the three hands. 2. **Draw phase**: Clockwise, each player draws 1 card, exposes it, and places it in one hand. 3. **Repeat** until all 13 cards are set. 4. **Showdown**: Compare Back vs Back, Middle vs Middle, Front vs Front against each opponent. 5. **Foul**: If Back < Middle or Middle < Front, you score 0 and pay 6 pts per opponent. 6. **Scoring**: 1 pt per hand won; 3 pt scoop bonus; royalties for straights, flushes, full houses, etc. 7. **Fantasyland**: QQ+ in Front (without fouling) gives 13 cards dealt at once on the next hand.',
